.json"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "125b930adbc81933b58b38886760ab94b8bf8fd24cd18ba2b9bce5c1c83a100e" "basis" 1065 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "125b930adbc81933b58b38886760ab94b8bf8fd24cd18ba2b9bce5c1c83a100e" "basis" 1065 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "125b930adbc81933b58b38886760ab94b8bf8fd24cd18ba2b9bce5c1c83a100e" "basis" 1065 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=2 \\\\ x-2y-5z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y+2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "125b930adbc81933b58b38886760ab94b8bf8fd24cd18ba2b9bce5c1c83a100e" "basis" 1065 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=5,y=3,z=0.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=5+3+0=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "125b930adbc81933b58b38886760ab94b8bf8fd24cd18ba2b9bce5c1c83a100e" "basis" 1065 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23" "basis" 1065 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_